# Playwright E2E artifacts
playwright-report/
test-results/
e2e/.auth/
e2e/.cache/
e2e/screenshots/

# Vitest coverage output (regenerated via `npm run test:coverage`)
coverage/

# Cleanup-branch baseline traces — captured locally for before/after diff
scripts/.baseline/

# One-off cleanup follow-up notes + pre-cleanup DB count snapshots. Historical
# artifacts archived under docs/audits/2026-05-26/; keep these dirs out of the
# tree so future local runs don't re-commit scratch files.
scripts/.followup/
scripts/backups/

# Claude agent isolation worktrees — created automatically by the Agent tool
# when isolation:"worktree" is used. They're not source we want to commit.
.claude/worktrees/

# Phase-0 audit baseline traces — useful locally for before/after comparison
# but ~10 MB of Playwright trace zips that would bloat the repo. Re-capture
# locally via Phase 0 protocol when needed (docs/audit/00-baseline.md §2).
docs/audits/**/baseline-traces/

# Knowledge-graph output from the /understand tooling — 16 MB of generated
# JSON across ~228 files, rebuilt on demand via `/understand`. Local-only.
.understand-anything/

# Audit screenshots — 431 PNGs / 48 MB of Playwright captures from the
# 2026-08-23 audit. The textual evidence (findings.json, reports, probe
# scripts) IS tracked; the images are re-capturable and would nearly double
# the repo. Same rationale as baseline-traces/ above.
docs/audits/**/screenshots/
docs/audits/**/*.png

# macOS folder-sync conflict copies — "Foo 2.jsx", "Bar 3.ts". This repo lives
# under ~/Desktop; its sync process duplicates files during branch switches
# (1,664 in one session). Byte-identical to their originals and never wanted in
# git. Also ignored by eslint.config.js so they cannot perturb the lint gate.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9][0-9].*
